{"title":"Risk Assessor Roadmap","role":"Risk Assessor","summary":"A Risk Assessor identifies hazards, evaluates the likelihood and potential consequences of incidents, determines risk levels, and recommends controls to reduce the probability or severity of accidents.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Fire Technology & Safety Engineering"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Risk Assessor identifies hazards, evaluates the likelihood and potential consequences of incidents, determines risk levels, and recommends controls to reduce the probability or severity of accidents."},{"type":"p","text":"For a Fire Technology & Safety Engineering graduate, the role commonly focuses on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fire hazards"},{"text":"Industrial safety"},{"text":"Process hazards"},{"text":"Emergency preparedness"},{"text":"Occupational safety"},{"text":"Chemical hazards"},{"text":"Building and workplace fire safety"},{"text":"Risk assessment and mitigation"},{"text":"Regulatory compliance"},{"text":"Emergency response"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The role can exist across manufacturing, oil & gas, chemicals, construction, infrastructure, logistics, power, mining, hospitals, commercial buildings, and consulting."},{"type":"p","text":"A strong Risk Assessor should move beyond checklist-based inspection and develop the ability to perform structured hazard identification, quantitative/qualitative risk analysis, consequence assessment, and risk-control design."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career Area","Potential Roles"],"rows":[[{"text":"Risk Assessment"},{"text":"Risk Assessor"}],[{"text":"Industrial Safety"},{"text":"Safety Engineer"}],[{"text":"Fire Safety"},{"text":"Fire Safety Engineer"}],[{"text":"Process Safety"},{"text":"Process Safety Engineer"}],[{"text":"HSE"},{"text":"HSE Engineer"}],[{"text":"Operational Risk"},{"text":"Operational Risk Analyst"}],[{"text":"Loss Prevention"},{"text":"Loss Prevention Engineer"}],[{"text":"Emergency Management"},{"text":"Emergency Preparedness Specialist"}],[{"text":"Safety Consulting"},{"text":"Safety / Risk Consultant"}],[{"text":"Compliance"},{"text":"Safety Compliance Engineer"}],[{"text":"Construction Safety"},{"text":"Construction Safety Engineer"}],[{"text":"EHS Analytics"},{"text":"EHS Data Analyst"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year-by-Year Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Engineering & Safety Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong fundamentals in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Engineering mathematics"},{"text":"Engineering physics"},{"text":"Engineering chemistry"},{"text":"Engineering mechanics"},{"text":"Electrical fundamentals"},{"text":"Engineering drawing"},{"text":"Basic programming"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Fire Science"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fire triangle"},{"text":"Fire tetrahedron"},{"text":"Heat transfer"},{"text":"Combustion"},{"text":"Ignition"},{"text":"Flame propagation"},{"text":"Flash point"},{"text":"Fire point"},{"text":"Auto-ignition temperature"},{"text":"Smoke generation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Safety Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hazard"},{"text":"Risk"},{"text":"Exposure"},{"text":"Incident"},{"text":"Accident"},{"text":"Near miss"},{"text":"Unsafe act"},{"text":"Unsafe condition"},{"text":"Control measure"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the difference:"},{"type":"h","text":"Hazard ≠ Risk"},{"type":"p","text":"A hazard is a potential source of harm, while risk considers the likelihood and consequence associated with that hazard."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Hazard Identification & Risk Assessment"},{"type":"p","text":"This is the core stage for the target career."},{"type":"h","text":"Hazard Identification"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to identify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"t